            <strong>CURSOR FITNESS is a real Amazon brand selling budget incline walking pads with handles, not running
            treadmills. The U20F 15% pad at $115.19 is the one to buy on price, the 18% pad at $151.98 if you need a 400 lb
            rating, and the 2-20% auto-incline treadmill at $284.99 if you want powered incline (Amazon, 27 Nov 2026).</strong>
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Who sells it:</strong> ten of the fourteen CURSOR FITNESS-branded listings we found were sold
            by a storefront called RUNHOME; the other four were sold by Woot. None was sold by Amazon.com.</li>
            <li><strong>Walking pads:</strong> $94.99 to $199.99 on 27 November 2026, mostly with side handles, a manual
            incline of 15 to 32%, top speeds of 5 to 7.5 mph and belts of 35.8 to 38.6 inches.</li>
            <li><strong>Folding treadmills:</strong> three listings with a 20% <a href="/best-auto-incline-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium" data-autolink>automatic incline</a>, $254.99 to $289.99, with
            42.5 to 44.1-inch belts and 8 to 8.7 mph.</li>
            <li><strong>Warranty:</strong> one year in every listing's product details that gives one; one listing states
            none. We found no brand-run warranty or returns page.</li>
            <li><strong>Prices today:</strong> eleven listings carried Amazon's "Black Friday Deal" label, open to all
            buyers, not Prime-only.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            If you are shopping on price, a CURSOR FITNESS pad belongs in the same comparison as the machines in our guide
            to the <a href="/best-walking-pads-with-incline/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">best walking pads with incline</a>.
            What you should not do is trust the incline in a CURSOR FITNESS title: three listings below give one figure in
            the title and another in the bullets.
          </p>
