            <summary><h3>Is CURSOR FITNESS a good treadmill brand?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              It is a legitimate budget brand on Amazon, with machines in stock, a one-year warranty on its listings and one main storefront, RUNHOME, behind them. Its pads are reasonable for incline walking with handles, but every belt is 44.1 inches or shorter and several listings contradict themselves, so they are not running treadmills.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Who sells CURSOR FITNESS treadmills?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              On 27 November 2026, ten of the fourteen CURSOR FITNESS-branded listings were sold by a storefront called RUNHOME and four by Woot. None was sold by Amazon.com. We found no brand-run store; a site at cursor-fitness.com links to Amazon and sells nothing itself.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What warranty comes with a CURSOR FITNESS walking pad?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Thirteen of the fourteen listings give one year in their product details; one variation listing states none. Only one listing explains the cover: one year for defects, with support through Amazon messaging. Keep the box and your order number.
